"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["The rapid rise in the price of ZEC has enlarged the monetary value of ZCG’s treasury to a much greater amount than ever before. This ZIP reduces the risks and pressure that come with large amounts of money, donates to the Network Sustainability Mechanism (providing increased long-term issuance), and accrues funds in a lockbox for future use by the Zcash community."]},{"tag":"p","children":["ZCG’s dashboard reports holdings of 91,452.98 ZEC and $8,796,224, against $2,417,165 of outstanding grant liabilities ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5","href":"#fn5"}]},". FPF reported $4,718,359 of ZCG expenses in the first half of 2026, about $9.4 million a year ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6","href":"#fn6"}]},". The 8% stream adds another 144 ZEC a day, 52,560 ZEC a year; at $1,300 per ZEC, that is about $68 million a year, more than seven times ZCG’s spending ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7","href":"#fn7"}]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":["ZCG’s treasury before and after the donation, at $1,300 per ZEC (details ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8","href":"#fn8"}]},"):"]},{"tag":"table","children":[{"tag":"thead","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"th","children":[]},{"tag":"th","children":["ZEC"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Dollars"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Value, less grant liabilities"]},{"tag":"th","children":["Years of spending at 2026 levels"]}]}]},{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["Before"]},{"tag":"td","children":["91,452.98"]},{"tag":"td","children":["$8,796,224"]},{"tag":"td","children":["$125.3 million"]},{"tag":"td","children":["13.3"]}]},{"tag":"tr","children":[{"tag":"td","children":["After"]},{"tag":"td","children":["41,452.98"]},{"tag":"td","children":["$8,796,224"]},{"tag":"td","children":["$60.3 million