{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖣"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["("],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mi","children":["h"]},{"tag":"mo","children":[")"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}}]},", and ZIP 237’s list of mechanisms for removal from circulation gains the source ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖣"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["("],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mi","children":["h"]},{"tag":"mo","children":[")"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}}]},", so that it is added to the NSM Value Balance."]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Anyone MAY send ZEC to the NSM donation address, and nothing sent there can be returned. Wallets SHOULD NOT offer it as an ordinary payment destination. Counts of circulating supply SHOULD exclude everything sent to it, before ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["A"]}]}," as well as after."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["The donation"],"id":"thedonation"},{"tag":"p","children":["The ZCG Committee SHALL cause 50,000 ZEC of the funds it administers to be sent to the NSM donation address, in one or more Mainnet transactions. It SHALL do so as soon as possible, and no later than 30 days after the date on which this ZIP is accepted by the Zcash community."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Since the funds ZCG administers are held by FPF, the ZCG Committee fulfills this obligation by directing FPF to create the transactions, as it directs FPF to make grant payments under ZIP 1015. Only FPF’s payments count toward the donation."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ZCG Committee SHALL publish the transaction identifier of each such transaction to the Zcash community promptly after it is mined."]},{"tag":"h3","children":["Changes to ZIPs 1015 and 1016"],"id":"changestozips1015and1016"},{"tag":"p","children":["In ZIP 1015’s section on ZCG ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["16"],"id":"fnref16","href":"#fn16"}]},", add: “ZCG funds MAY also be used for the donation to the Network Sustainability Mechanism that [this ZIP] specifies. That donation is not a grant.”"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In ZIP 1016’s section on ZCG ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["17"],"id":"fnref17","href":"#fn17"}]},", end ZCG’s funding stream at this ZIP’s activation height, and state that from then until the third halving the same 8% goes into the Future Dev and Legal Defense Fund Lockbox, as this ZIP specifies. In its section on the Coinholder-Controlled Fund, give the 12% stream’s duration by ",{"tag":"code","children":["FS_CCF_H3"]},"’s own start and end heights in ZIP 214, which this ZIP leaves unchanged."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Rationale"],"id":"rationale"},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["A lockbox of its own."]}," The 8% is set aside, issued but locked, for future development and legal defense, and a future ZIP decides how it is spent. A separate balance keeps it apart from the Deferred Dev Fund Lockbox’s purpose and disbursement rules, and like that lockbox it needs no custodians or keys."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["A donation by address."]}," NU7 deploys ZIP 237’s NSM but no way for a transaction to remove ZEC from circulation directly: it deploys neither ZIP 233 nor ZIP 234 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["18"],"id":"fnref18","href":"#fn18"}]}," ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"id":"fnref11:1","href":"#fn11"}]},". Sending to an address that no one can spend from lets the donation happen now; at ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["A"]}]},", it moves into the NSM, with every earlier payment to the address. The consensus change is small: no new transaction fields, address formats, or wallet changes. Payments from anyone count, so the address serves every donor. If ZIP 233 is deployed later, both mechanisms add to the same NSM Value Balance."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["The donation’s size."]}," 50,000 ZEC is about 55% of ZCG’s ZEC. Anyone can check its payment on the chain, and ZCG keeps the rest of its treasury and its grants program."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Accounting."]}," The lockbox’s balance stays in the Issued Supply. A donation moves value from the transparent pool to the NSM Value Balance in the same block. Both keep ZIP 237’s invariant: in each block from NU7 on, the Issued Supply plus the NSM Value Balance grows by exactly the scheduled block subsidy."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"strong","children":["Other proposals."]}," ZIP draft #1414 sends the 8% stream to the NSM ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["19"],"id":"fnref19","href":"#fn19"}]},", and draft #1423 winds ZCG down ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["20"],"id":"fnref20","href":"#fn20"}]},". Where they overlap with this ZIP, they are alternatives to it."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Deployment"],"id":"deployment"},{"tag":"p","children":["The lockbox and the NSM donation address are consensus changes, proposed for a network upgrade after NU7 that activates before height ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["E"]}]},"; that upgrade’s deployment ZIP sets ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["A"]}]}," for each network ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["21"],"id":"fnref21","href":"#fn21"}]},". The donation needs no network upgrade: it is due within 30 days of this ZIP’s acceptance."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Reference implementation"],"id":"referenceimplementation"},{"tag":"p","children":["None yet."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["References"],"id":"references"},{"tag":"hr","children":[]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Information on BCP 14 — “RFC 2119: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels” and “RFC 8174: Ambiguity of Uppercase vs Lowercase in RFC 2119 Key Words”"],"href":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/bcp14"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref1"}]}],"id":"fn1"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Zcash Protocol Specification"],"href":"https://zips.z.cash/protocol/protocol.pdf"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref2"}]}],"id":"fn2"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 1015: Block Subsidy Allocation for Non-Direct Development Funding"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-1015"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref3"}]}],"id":"fn3"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 237: Network Sustainability Mechanism: Halving-Preserving Issuance"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0237"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref4"}]}],"id":"fn4"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Zcash Community Grants website"],"href":"https://zcashcommunitygrants.org/"}," and its linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zcash Community Grants + Coinholder Grants Dashboard"],"href":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1FQ28rDCyRW0TiNxrm3rgD8ai2KGUsXAjPieQmI1kKKg/edit?usp=sharing"},", accessed October 26, 2026. The recorded inputs are 91,452.98 ZEC, USD 8,796,224, and USD 2,417,165 in grant liabilities. The dashboard’s block reference is 3,526,011 (October 21, 2026, 22:37:53 UTC), and the worksheet is marked “Updates required”. The figures are reported dashboard inputs and have not been independently reconciled. ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref5"}]}],"id":"fn5"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Financial Privacy Foundation: Q2 2026 Report, p. 5 (ZCG statistics, with total expenses for Q1 and Q2 2026)"],"href":"https://9ba4718c-5c73-47c3-a024-4fc4e5278803.usrfiles.com/ugd/9ba471_0836532577dd4f0eab3cf5080820e622.pdf"},". Q2’s total includes $1,216,687 of Discretionary Fund usage, versus $54,108 in Q1, so neither quarter alone indicates recurring spending. ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref6"}]}],"id":"fn6"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["The 8% of a 1.5625 ZEC block subsidy, at 1,152 blocks of 75 seconds a day: ",{"tag":"code","children":["0.08 * 1.5625 * 1,152 = 144"]}," ZEC a day, ",{"tag":"code","children":["144 * 365 = 52,560"]}," ZEC a year; at USD 1,300 per ZEC, USD 68,328,000 a year. ZIP 218’s 25-second blocks, each with a third of the subsidy, leave the daily amount the same, apart from rounding. Annual spending: ",{"tag":"code","children":["(1,530,844 + 3,187,515) * 2 = 9,436,718"]}," USD, from the Q2 2026 report. ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref7"}]}],"id":"fn7"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":["From the dashboard figures above, at USD 1,300 per ZEC: before the donation, ",{"tag":"code","children":["91,452.98 * 1,300 + 8,796,224 - 2,417,165 = 125,267,933"]}," USD; after it, ",{"tag":"code","children":["41,452.98 * 1,300 + 8,796,224 - 2,417,165 = 60,267,933"]}," USD. Years of spending divide these by the 2026 rate of USD 9,436,718 a year. The figures assume no conversion costs and no further receipts, returns, or obligations beyond the dashboard’s grant liabilities. ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref8"}]}],"id":"fn8"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 214: Consensus rules for a Zcash Development Fund"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0214"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref9"}]}],"id":"fn9"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 218: 25-second Block Target Spacing"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0218"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref10"}]}],"id":"fn10"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 259: Deployment of the NU7 Network Upgrade"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0259"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref11"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref11:1"}]}],"id":"fn11"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 207: Funding Streams"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0207"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref12"}]}],"id":"fn12"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 2008: Update to ",{"tag":"code","children":["FS_FPF_ZCG_H3"]}," address list"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-2008"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref13"}]}],"id":"fn13"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 2001: Lockbox Funding Streams"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-2001"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref14"}]}],"id":"fn14"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 209: Prohibit Out-of-Range Chain Value Pool Balances"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-0209"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref15"}]}],"id":"fn15"},{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ZIP 1015: Block Subsidy Allocation for Non-Direct Development Funding — Zcash Community Grants"],"href":"?view=governance&section=zips&record=zip-1015#zcash-community-grants-zcg"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["↩︎"],"href":"#fnref16